WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.216 --> 00:00:19.261
The White Rabbit soon noticed Alice hunting for his gloves and fan.

2
00:00:23.902 --> 00:00:26.403
He called out to her in an angry voice.

3
00:00:27.703 --> 00:00:30.784
"Mary Ann, what are you doing here?

4
00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:36.560
Run home right now, and fetch me a pair of gloves and a fan!

5
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.544
Hurry!" Alice knew that the rabbit had mistaken her for someone else.

6
00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:48.088
But he sounded so angry that she ran where he was pointing.

7
00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.511
She didn't try to explain his mistake to him.

8
00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:54.933
"He probably thinks I'm his servant," she thought.

9
00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:58.496
"He'll be surprised when he finds out who I am.

10
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.921
But he's so angry right now that I'd better find his gloves and fan."

11
00:01:05.922 --> 00:01:08.703
Alice soon came upon a neat little house.

12
00:01:09.843 --> 00:01:12.224
On the door was a brass sign that said W.

13
00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:17.465
Rabbit. She hurried inside and closed the front door.

14
00:01:17.485 --> 00:01:23.007
"How strange to be sent on an errand by a rabbit."

15
00:01:23.747 --> 00:01:24.447
Alice laughed.

16
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.868
"Soon Dinah will be sending me on errands too!"

17
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.722
Alice entered a room with a table near the window.

18
00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:38.925
On the table lay a fan and a pair of white gloves.

19
00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:40.566
Alice picked them up.

20
00:01:44.328 --> 00:01:47.330
She was about to leave when she spotted a bottle on the floor.

21
00:01:52.894 --> 00:01:58.177
This time there was no label saying, Drink Me, but Alice uncorked the bottle anyway.

22
00:01:58.197 --> 00:02:04.826
"Whenever I eat or drink anything today, something interesting happens," she thought.

23
00:02:05.786 --> 00:02:06.647
She took a sip.

24
00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:12.591
"I hope this will make me grow again because I'm tired of being so small."

25
00:02:13.452 --> 00:02:18.175
That is exactly what happened and much faster than Alice expected.

26
00:02:18.956 --> 00:02:23.679
Before she had drunk half the bottle, her head was pressing against the ceiling.

27
00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:25.880
She quickly put down the bottle.

28
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.341
"That's enough!

29
00:02:28.062 --> 00:02:30.704
I hope I won't grow anymore because I can't get out the door.

30
00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.081
I wish I hadn't drunk so much."

31
00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:36.623
But it was too late for that.

32
00:02:37.464 --> 00:02:41.026
Alice went on growing and soon had to kneel on the floor.

33
00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:45.409
In another minute she had to lie with one foot up the chimney.

34
00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.051
She stuck one arm out the window.

35
00:02:48.071 --> 00:02:51.113
"There's no more room for me!"

36
00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:52.374
Alice wailed.

37
00:02:53.015 --> 00:02:54.656
Luckily she stopped growing.

38
00:02:55.656 --> 00:03:00.020
But she was very uncomfortable, being squashed inside the White Rabbit's house.

39
00:03:01.032 --> 00:03:03.894
"It was much nicer at home," Alice said.

40
00:03:03.914 --> 00:03:08.978
"I wasn't always changing size, and mice and rabbits weren't ordering me around.

41
00:03:08.998 --> 00:03:11.920
I wish I hadn't gone down that rabbit hole.

42
00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:17.144
And yet and yet this is quite an adventure.

43
00:03:17.845 --> 00:03:19.706
I used to think fairy tales weren't real.

44
00:03:20.687 --> 00:03:22.808
And now I seem to be in the middle of one!

45
00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:30.990
Maybe someone will write a book about me—" Suddenly Alice heard an angry voice outside.

46
00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:36.013
"Mary Ann, where are you!"

47
00:03:36.393 --> 00:03:37.434
the White Rabbit called.

48
00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:46.079
He tried to open his front door, but Alice's elbow was pressing hard against it.

49
00:03:52.202 --> 00:03:55.164
I'll go through a window," the White Rabbit said.

50
00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.901
"No, you won't," Alice said.

51
00:04:00.221 --> 00:04:03.203
She waited until she heard the White Rabbit under the window.

52
00:04:04.423 --> 00:04:06.404
Then she tried to grab him.

53
00:04:08.685 --> 00:04:11.306
The White Rabbit shrieked and ran away.

54
00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:14.728
"Pat! Pat!

55
00:04:15.148 --> 00:04:15.968
Where are you?"

56
00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.770
"Right here!

57
00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.911
Digging potatoes in the garden," a man replied.

58
00:04:22.931 --> 00:04:27.081
"Pat, what's that in the window?"

59
00:04:32.463 --> 00:04:35.524
There was a pause while the gardener looked at the house.

60
00:04:41.226 --> 00:04:42.627
Looks like an arm to me."

61
00:04:42.647 --> 00:04:45.568
"An arm?

62
00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.009
Who's ever seen an arm that big?

63
00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:49.430
Take it away!"

64
00:04:51.851 --> 00:04:54.952
Alice waved her arm around and heard some whispering.

65
00:04:55.821 --> 00:05:01.862
Then all was silent for a while—until a crowd began gathering under the window.
